  _menuDescription: Last seen on hamster wheel.  Hamster wheel is also missing.
  _funFacts:
  - _fact: Guinea pigs aren't actually from Guinea, nor are they related to pigs.
      They are highly vocal South American rodents known for unique behaviors like
      "popcorning" (acrobatic jumps of excitement).
  - _fact: Guinea pigs eyes are positioned to give them a nearly 340-degree field
      of vision, allowing them to spot predators from almost any angle.
  - _fact: "Guinea pigs have an uneven number of toes\u2014four on their front feet
      and three on their back feet."
  - _fact: As prey animals, guinea pigs rarely enter deep sleep. They get by on quick
      30-second to 5-minute power naps, totaling only about 4 hours of sleep a day.
